<AtTheTable>

Use a two-card hit chance when both future cards will actually be dealt for the decision being priced, such as an all-in. Facing a flop bet with later betting still possible, distinguish seeing one card from paying again on the turn. Completing the draw and winning the pot are different questions.

</AtTheTable>

<QuantCorner>

An event’s horizon is part of its definition. A two-period chance cannot be substituted for a one-period chance without changing the decision being evaluated. Simulating the exact horizon is a useful check on a shortcut.

</QuantCorner>
